# Design System

## Brand
Skill Bridge is an elite Global Talent Visa **consultancy** — never frame it as an immigration agency.

## Aesthetic references
Linear.app, Vercel, Stripe, Notion, Framer, Apple. Premium, trustworthy, clean, editorial, minimal.

## Layout
- Max width: `1280px` (`max-w-7xl` / container utility)
- 12-column mental grid; generous white space
- Section padding: `py-20 md:py-28` unless a hero needs more
- Rounded cards: `rounded-2xl` / `rounded-xl`
- Soft shadows only (`shadow-sm` / custom soft tokens)

## Color
- Brand blue: `#2563EB` → CSS `--primary` (`oklch(0.546 0.215 262.88)`).
- Use Tailwind: `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `border-primary`, `bg-primary/10`, `ring-primary`.
- Default `Button` already uses `bg-primary text-primary-foreground`.
- Eyebrows, stats, active nav, timeline markers, and key CTAs should use primary.
- Neutrals stay cool near-white / near-black. No purple-on-white, no cream/terracotta, no neon glow.
- Glass (`backdrop-blur`) only on navbar-on-scroll and auth cards.

## Typography
- Geist Sans for UI; Geist Mono sparingly for labels/accents
- Large display headlines (`text-4xl`–`text-6xl`), clear hierarchy
- Body: comfortable leading (`leading-relaxed`)

## Banned
- WordPress / TemplateMonster looks
- Typical immigration-site chrome (flags, passport stamps, cartoon planes)
- Generic AI gradients, purple glows, cartoon/stock illustrations
- Cheesy motion, emoji decoration, pill-stat strips in heroes
- Cards in the hero; inset/floating hero media cards when a full-bleed plane is intended

## Imagery
High-quality Unsplash photos via `next/image`. Professionals, workspaces, editorial headshots. Never AI illustrations.
